  1: # FileSentinel DLP — Secure File Transfer Monitoring System
  2: 
  3: A Python-based Blue Team security tool designed to monitor filesystem activity in real time, detect unauthorized movement of sensitive or restricted files, verify file integrity via cryptographic hashing (SHA-256), generate policy alerts, and stream security telemetry to a local SPLUNK-style dashboard and **native Windows desktop application**.
  4: 
  5: ---
  6: *In other words, an easy to use and efficient (fun) way to track files if you deal with a lot of them on daily basis.*
  7: 
  8: ---
  9: 
 10: ## 🎯 Objectives & Capabilities
 11: 
 12: - **Real-Time Filesystem Monitoring:** Tracks `CREATED`, `MODIFIED`, `MOVED`, and `DELETED` file events across configured target directories.
 13: - **Unauthorized Movement & Exfiltration Detection:**
 14:   - Maintains strict policy lists of sensitive directories and high-risk file types.
 15:   - Detects suspicious outbound transfer vectors (USB / removable media, UNC network shares, cloud storage sync folders).
 16: - **Cryptographic File Integrity Verification:**
 17:   - Computes pre- and post-transfer hash digests (SHA-256 / SHA-512 / MD5) using Python's built-in `hashlib`.
 18:   - Flags tampering, corruption, or unexpected content alterations (`INTACT` vs `TAMPERED`).
 19: - **Telemetry, Alerting & Audit Logging:**
 20:   - 3-tier severity classification: `INFO`, `WARNING`, `CRITICAL`.
 21:   - Structured, machine-readable JSON-line audit logs in `logs/audit.log`.
 22:   - Real-time terminal alerts via `colorama` with high-visibility banners for policy violations.
 23: - **Native Windows Desktop Application:**
 24:   - Runs inside a dedicated native desktop window (powered by `pywebview`).
 25:   - **System Tray Icon (`pystray`):** Runs continuously in the background near the clock; closing the window minimizes to the tray.
 26:   - **Native Toast Notifications:** Displays Windows slide-in alert notifications for `WARNING` and `CRITICAL` events.
 27:   - Right-click tray menu to open dashboard, pause/resume monitoring, or export audit reports.
 28: - **SPLUNK-Style Local Dashboard with Vertical Chat Reports:**
 29:   - Local Flask web UI (`http://127.0.0.1:5000`) with auto-refreshing telemetry, searchable/filterable logs, and live alert feeds.
 30:   - **Interactive Incident Chat Drawer:** Clicking any log event row opens a vertical report in chat block form (System alert, Telemetry breakdown, SHA-256 hash inspection, and SOC blue-team advice).
 31:   - Zero external network dependencies (100% localhost).
 32: - **Standalone `.exe` & Windows `.msi` Installer:**
 33:   - Compiled portable executable `FileSentinel.exe` (run directly with zero Python installation required).
 34:   - Official Windows Installer `FileSentinel-Setup.msi` with desktop/start menu shortcuts and clean uninstallation.
 35: - **Noise Suppression & Write-Burst Debouncing:**
 36:   - Eliminates duplicate operating system write-buffer flushes during large file transfers.
 37:   - Prevents recursive log feedback loops.
 38: 
 39: ---
 40: 
 41: ## 🏗️ Architecture & Workflow
 42: 
 43: ```
 44: [ Filesystem Event ] (watchdog)
 45:         │
 46:         ▼
 47: [ Noise & Internal Filter ] ──> Ignore own logs, .git, OS metadata (~$*, .tmp, desktop.ini)
 48:         │
 49:         ▼
 50: [ Write-Burst Debounce ] ────> Suppress rapid OS buffer flushes within debounce window
 51:         │
 52:         ▼
 53: [ Event Classification ] ────> Check Sensitive Extensions / Directories & Suspicious Destinations
 54:         │                       ├── CRITICAL: Sensitive file moved to USB/Cloud/Network or Deleted
 55:         │                       ├── WARNING : Sensitive file Created/Modified
 56:         │                       └── INFO    : Normal file activity
 57:         │
 58:         ▼
 59: [ Integrity Hashing ] ───────> Compute SHA-256 (pre/post transfer comparison)
 60:         │
 61:         ├───> [ Structured Logger ] ───> logs/audit.log (JSON Lines) + Console
 62:         ├───> [ Alerter ] ─────────────> logs/alerts.log + Terminal Banner
 63:         ├───> [ Native Toast Notifier ]> Windows Notification Center
 64:         └───> [ Desktop / Web UI ] ────> Native Desktop Window or http://localhost:5000
 65: ```
