185: ## 🛑 How to Stop / Exit the Program
186: 
187: ### When Running the Desktop App (`--desktop` or `FileSentinel.exe`):
188: To exit the application, use any of the following convenient options:
189: 1. **Close the Window (`X`):** Simply click the close button on the desktop window. FileSentinel shuts down all background threads, stops monitoring, and exits cleanly.
190: 2. **Press `Ctrl + C`:** If launched from a PowerShell or Command Prompt terminal, pressing `Ctrl + C` immediately terminates all monitoring and Flask threads.
191: 3. **System Tray Menu:** Right-click the FileSentinel shield icon in the system tray and select **Exit FileSentinel**.
192: 
193: ### When Running in Terminal Mode (`--monitor`):
194: * Press **`Ctrl + C`** in your PowerShell or Command Prompt window. The watchdog observer will flush any remaining logs and shut down gracefully.
195: 
196: ### Emergency Force-Stop:
197: If you need to force-terminate any lingering processes from PowerShell:
198: ```powershell
199: Stop-Process -Name FileSentinel, python -Force -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue
200: ```
